15041","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.198839,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.00111862,"nucleus_score":-1.46097,"pct_ad":0.244311,"pct_control":0.257138,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.986262,"donor_log2fc":-0.0410772,"donor_lfcse":0.0959486,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-4.62045e-06},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_symbol":"KCNIP3","gene_symbol_current":"KCNIP3","gene_id":"ENSG00000115041","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"higher in AD","nucleus_padj":0.505983,"nucleus_log2fc":0.248203,"nucleus_score":1.26665,"pct_ad":0.17033,"pct_control":0.155556,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.976536,"donor_log2fc":0.234599,"donor_lfcse":0.174809,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.00159234}],"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000115041","entrez_id":["30818"],"uniprot":["Q9Y2W7"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a member of the family of voltage-gated potassium (Kv) channel-interacting proteins, which belong to the recoverin branch of the EF-hand superfamily. Members of this family are small calcium binding proteins containing EF-hand-like domains. They are integral subunit components of native Kv4 channel complexes that may regulate A-type currents, and hence neuronal excitability, in response to changes in intracellular calcium. The encoded protein also functions as a calcium-regulated transcriptional repressor, and interacts with presenilins. Alternatively spliced transcript variants encoding different isoforms have been described. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9Y2W7","text":"Calcium-dependent transcriptional repressor that binds to the DRE element of genes including PDYN and FOS. Affinity for DNA is reduced upon binding to calcium and enhanced by binding to magnesium. Seems to be involved in nociception (By similarity). Regulatory subunit of Kv4/D (Shal)-type voltage-gated rapidly inactivating A-type potassium channels, such as KCND2/Kv4.2 and KCND3/Kv4.3. Modulates channel expression at the cell membrane, gating characteristics, inactivation kinetics and rate of recovery from inactivation in a calcium-dependent and isoform-specific manner. May play a role in the regulation of PSEN2 proteolytic processing and apoptosis. Together with PSEN2 involved in modulation of amyloid-beta formation."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}